                        <details className="bg-white rounded-xl border border-slate-200 shadow-sm px-5 py-3 text-sm text-slate-600">
                            <summary className="cursor-pointer text-sm font-black text-[#00468B] uppercase tracking-widest">How these numbers are worked out</summary>
                            <ul className="mt-3 space-y-1.5 list-disc pl-5">
                                <li>Every time Shift Start puts someone in an area it saves a row. A new row for the same person ends the one before it.</li>
                                <li><b>Times assigned</b> counts one shift in one area once, even if the person was moved back and forth within it. A night shift (6 PM to 6 AM) counts for the day it began, so the early-morning hours stay with it.</li>
                                <li><b>Hours</b> run from the start of an assignment to its end time. Shift Start only stamps an end time when someone is moved, so the last assignment of a shift has none: it runs to the next move in that shift, or to the end of the shift (6 PM for days, 6 AM for nights). Never more than {EMP_MAX_ROW_MS / 3600000} hours for one assignment, and a move that is undone within {EMP_SLIP_MS / 60000} minutes is ignored.</li>
                                <li><b>Days worked</b> and hours leave out PTO, sick days and no call, no shows. Late and left early are counted on their own.</li>
                                <li><b>Strongest area</b> is where the person spent the most hours, once they have at least {EMP_MIN_SHIFTS_FOR_STRONGEST} shifts there. It reflects time spent, not how well the work went.</li>
